#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Fills the test couple's account on this worktree's local backend with made-up
# content for App Store screenshots, in English or Norwegian.
#
#   scripts/app-store-content --locale en|nb [--drawing <file.pkdrawing>]
#       [--drawing-canvas-side 320] [--drawing-strokes N --drawing-points N
#        --drawing-bounds x,y,width,height] [--partner-answer-only | --chat-only]
#
# --partner-answer-only has only Elena answer today's question and leaves the
# chat out, so Home still invites Hjalmar to answer. A later run with
# --chat-only answers for Hjalmar if he has not, and adds the chat.
#
# Run it on a backend that holds only the paired test couple from
# scripts/test-couple. The first account becomes Hjalmar and the second Elena.
# Screenshots are taken as Hjalmar. Every write goes through the app's own
# Convex functions, called as one of the two accounts, so the server's rules
# apply. Steps that already ran are skipped, so it is safe to run again.
#
# It seeds names and profile photos, the start date (504 days ago, past the
# 500-day mark), a countdown 12 days out, today's question answered by Hjalmar
# and then Elena with a chat about it, three memories with photos, a Ludo game
# waiting for Hjalmar's move, a Draw & Guess round where Elena drew GUESS_DRAWING
# for Hjalmar to guess, a note on Home from each, both locations on the Home
# map, and with --drawing a widget drawing from Elena.
#
# The server picks a day's question at random, and each partner can skip it 30
# times a day. The script skips until today's question is QUESTION_KEY. When the
# skips run out, it runs the operator mutation daily:reset_daily_challenge_for_testing
# with `npx convex run`, which clears today's question and skips, and tries again.
# Two more steps do not run as an account, because the app's functions cannot do
# them: the couple's streak (STREAK_DAYS answered days in a row)
# and the drawing's time (--drawing-time, so the widget and the Home card show a
# morning time beside the 9:41 status bar). Both rewrite one table on the local
# backend with `npx convex data` and `npx convex import --replace`. These steps
# refuse to run unless backend/.env.local names the same local backend as
# ios/local.xcconfig. Seed once per locale and capture every screen from that one
# seeding, so the drawing shows the same time everywhere.
#
# The drawing is PKDrawing.dataRepresentation() bytes. Without the stroke count,
# point count and bounds it reads them from the file with a small PencilKit
# program it compiles with swiftc. The last stdout line is a JSON object with the
# ids the screenshot deep links need, the Draw & Guess word, the countdown's
# title, which the capture script finds the Home countdown card by, and Elena's
# Clerk subject, which scripts/capture-app-store-screenshots.py uses to show
# Elena at the Ludo table.
#
# It reads CLERK_DEV_SECRET_KEY and CLERK_DEV_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN from the
# api.paeonia.no env the way scripts/test-couple does. Tokens are never printed.
import argparse
